'' vendor/pcre2 -- PCRE2 10.49, the Perl-compatible regular expression library in C, its 8-bit
'' library (UTF-8 and bytes), with Unicode support and the JIT, as one import:
''
''     #import "vendor/pcre2" link dynamic        (or 'link static', or neither)
''
'' Every routine, type and constant of pcre2.h is then callable as PCRE2 documents it,
'' unqualified, by its generic name -- pcre2_compile, pcre2_match, pcre2_match_data,
'' PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED -- each a #define of the 8-bit name the library exports
'' (pcre2_compile_8), as pcre2.h gives them with PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH 8. There is no 16- or
'' 32-bit library: a ustring is matched as UTF-8 (PCRE2_UTF).
''
'' THE HEADER is pcre2_8.ti, translated by 'tiko c2t' and committed. pcre2.h declares its API
'' inside list macros that it pastes together three times, which c2t cannot translate, so
'' flatten.py first writes the 8-bit expansion as plain C -- pcre2_8.h, the file the banner
'' names by SHA-256 -- and c2t translates that. pcre2-residue.ti holds by hand what the
'' translation could not carry: PCRE2_DATE.
''
'' A short match, the pattern compiled once and its match data sized from it:
''
''     dim as int32 errc
''     dim as PCRE2_SIZE erroff
''     dim as string pat = "(\d+)-(\d+)", s = "pages 12-48"
''     dim as pcre2_code ptr re = pcre2_compile( strptr( pat ), len( pat ), 0, @errc, @erroff, 0 )
''     dim as pcre2_match_data ptr md = pcre2_match_data_create_from_pattern( re, 0 )
''     if pcre2_match( re, strptr( s ), len( s ), 0, 0, md, 0 ) > 0 then
''         dim as PCRE2_SIZE ptr ov = pcre2_get_ovector_pointer( md )
''         print mid( s, ov[2] + 1, ov[3] - ov[2] )        ' 12
''     end if
''     pcre2_match_data_free( md ) : pcre2_code_free( re )
''
'' A pattern or subject is a PCRE2_SPTR (const uint8 ptr): strptr( s ) passes as one, a string
'' literal does not -- put it in a string first. The ovector's offsets are 0-based byte offsets. What pcre2_substring_get_* returns is
'' PCRE2's to free: pcre2_substring_free. pcre2_jit_compile( re, PCRE2_JIT_COMPLETE ) makes
'' later pcre2_match calls on that pattern run the JIT code.
''
'' A PATTERN FROM OUTSIDE THE PROGRAM can take exponential time: PCRE2 backtracks. Bound it
'' with a match context: pcre2_set_match_limit (default 10,000,000 steps), which the JIT obeys
'' too; pcre2_set_depth_limit and pcre2_set_heap_limit (default 20,000,000 KiB, about 20 GB),
'' which only the interpreter does. A match that reaches one returns an error code.
'' pcre2_dfa_match is NOT a way out: it does not backtrack, but its time still grows steeply with
'' the subject -- (a+)+$ against 1,000 characters took half a minute -- and a match limit of
'' 100,000 did not stop it.
''
'' THE LIBRARY: with 'link static' PCRE2 is linked into the program; with 'link dynamic' --
'' and when no '#import' says, which is this package's default -- the shared library, which
'' tiko copies beside the program: pcre2.dll, pcre2_linux_x86_64.so on Linux, or
'' pcre2_macos_arm64.dylib on macOS.
#module "pcre2"

public #include once "pcre2_8.ti"
public #include once "pcre2-residue.ti"

#ifdef TIKO_LINK_STATIC
    #foreignlib PCRE2 static "lib/pcre2"
#else
    #foreignlib PCRE2 dynamic "lib/pcre2"
#endif
